  "question": {
    "text": "A line passing through the point $\\mathrm{A}(-2,0)$, touches the parabola $P: y^2=x-2$ at the point $B$ in the first quadrant. The area, of the region bounded by the line AB , parabola P and the x -axis, is :-",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "LHUav",
      "text": "$\\frac{7}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "CcwkI",
      "text": "$2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "q8ZAQ",
      "text": "$\\frac{8}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "nFzMx",
      "text": "$3$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Tangent<br/>$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& y=m(x+2) \\\\\n& y^2=x-2 \\\\\n& (m(n+2))^2=n-2 \\\\\n& m^2 x^2+\\left(4 m^2-1\\right) x+\\left(4 m^2+2\\right)=0 \\\\\n& D=0 \\\\\n& \\left(4 m^2-1\\right)^2-4 m^2\\left(4 m^2+2\\right)=0 \\\\\n& m=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\\n& y=\\frac{1}{4}(n+2)<br/>\\end{aligned}$<br/>and point of tangency $(6,2)$<br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/fO_xQwfS6yJmk1Vbn_d7nzoOlRl2BydN3-YN2hTy9-o.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& \\text { Area } A=\\int_0^2\\left(\\left(y^2+2\\right)-(4 y-2)\\right) d y \\\\\n& A=\\frac{8}{3}<br/>\\end{aligned}$<br/>option (3)",
    "image": null
  },
